    {
      "id": "apt3040_lecture_notes",
      "course_code": "APT3040 / SWE3020",
      "title": "USIU-Africa SST Lecture Notes: Enterprise Telemetry, Cloud ERP & Zero-Trust Security",
      "content": "Enterprise systems and real-time predictive telemetry architectures reduce supply chain stockout latency across East African distribution networks. Cloud ERP migration lowers upfront capital hardware expenditure for medium-sized retail enterprises in Nairobi and Kenya, though bandwidth reliability and vendor lock-in remain operational risks. Zero-trust cybersecurity governance enforces continuous device posture verification, role-based access control (RBAC), multi-factor authentication (MFA), and AES-256 encryption across mobile money microservices and higher education portals. Key regional scholarship includes Kamau et al. (2024), Ochieng & Wambui (2023), Njoroge et al. (2024), Mutua (2023), Kariuki (2022), and Otieno (2024).",
