      "id": "bus4010_case_brief",
      "course_code": "BUS4010 / MBA6010",
      "title": "Chandaria School of Business (CSB) Case Brief: Strategic Management in East Africa",
      "content": "Strategic diagnosis in Kenyan and East African markets requires rigorous application of SWOT (Strengths, Weaknesses, Opportunities, Threats), PESTEL (Political, Economic, Social, Technological, Environmental, Legal), Porter's Five Forces, and Value Chain Analysis. Financial and operational justification must quantify return on investment (ROI), profit margins, revenue growth, cost efficiency, and capital allocation in KES or USD. Actionable recommendations must include a phased implementation timeline, stakeholder alignment, and risk mitigation matrix.",
